# NORTH — the two PUBLIC values the web client needs at build time.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, or paste the same two
# values into your host's environment-variable settings for a deployment
# (Vercel: Settings → Environment Variables; Netlify: Site configuration →
# Environment variables). They are read at BUILD time, so a change needs a
# redeploy, not just a restart.
#
# Both values are public by design — they ship inside the JavaScript bundle and
# are protected by row-level security in the database, not by being secret.
# Get them from Supabase → Project Settings → API (see SETUP.md §1).
#
# NEVER put the `service_role` key here: it bypasses RLS and would hand every
# visitor full read/write access to every account.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
